Source: shift-layout
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Florian Loitsch <florian@toit.io>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/floitsch/keyboard_layout

Package: shift-layout
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, systemd, udev, xkb-data (>= 2.46)
Description: shifted US and Dvorak keyboard layouts
 Installs custom XKB layouts with unshifted punctuation on the digit row and
 hardware-database remaps for the original Carbon X1 and a Dell Precision 5490.

Package: shift-layout-dell-dvorak
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, shift-layout (= ${source:Version})
Description: internal Dell Dvorak remap with external US keyboards
 Translates the Dell Precision 5490 internal keyboard to Dvorak keycodes while
 preserving its physical modifier remaps. Select us_shifted in the desktop
 to get shifted Dvorak internally and shifted US on external keyboards.
 Do not combine this package with a Dvorak desktop layout.

Package: shift-layout-mouse
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, shift-layout (= ${source:Version})
Recommends: qml6-module-org-kde-plasma-plasma5support
Description: stateful mouse gesture proxy for shift-layout
 Proxies the supported 2.4G mouse through virtual mouse and keyboard devices,
 turning its back button into persistent Meta and button-scrolling gestures.
 The hardened system service runs as root to access input devices and uinput.
